Here's a vocabulary review screen: a ten-card flip deck on the left and a progress panel on the right.

<a2ui-json>
[
  {
    "version": "v0.9.1",
    "createSurface": {
      "surfaceId": "vocab-flashcards",
      "catalogId": "https://a2uicatalog.ai/catalog/c-learning.json"
    }
  },
  {
    "version": "v0.9.1",
    "updateComponents": {
      "surfaceId": "vocab-flashcards",
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "component": "columns",
          "cols": 2,
          "gap": "2rem",
          "align": "top",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "page_header",
                  "title": "Vocabulary Review",
                  "subtitle": "Ten words to flip through. Read the word, recall its meaning, then flip to check.",
                  "icon": "📚",
                  "tag": "10 cards",
                  "accent": "#4f46e5",
                  "meta": [
                    { "label": "Deck", "value": "Advanced English" },
                    { "label": "Cards", "value": "10" }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "flashcard_deck",
                  "accent": "#4f46e5",
                  "label_front": "WORD",
                  "label_back": "MEANING",
                  "cards": [
                    { "front": "Ephemeral", "back": "Lasting a very short time. \"The ephemeral beauty of cherry blossoms.\"" },
                    { "front": "Ubiquitous", "back": "Present or found everywhere. \"Smartphones have become ubiquitous.\"" },
                    { "front": "Candid", "back": "Truthful and straightforward; frank. \"She gave a candid account of the mistake.\"" },
                    { "front": "Meticulous", "back": "Showing great attention to detail. \"He kept meticulous records.\"" },
                    { "front": "Resilient", "back": "Able to recover quickly from difficulty. \"Children are often remarkably resilient.\"" },
                    { "front": "Ambiguous", "back": "Open to more than one interpretation. \"The ending of the film was deliberately ambiguous.\"" },
                    { "front": "Pragmatic", "back": "Dealing with things sensibly and realistically. \"We need a pragmatic solution.\"" },
                    { "front": "Benevolent", "back": "Well-meaning and kindly. \"A benevolent donor funded the library.\"" },
                    { "front": "Lucid", "back": "Expressed clearly; easy to understand. \"She wrote a lucid summary of the research.\"" },
                    { "front": "Tenacious", "back": "Holding firmly to a goal; persistent. \"A tenacious reporter chasing the story.\"" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "text": "Your progress"
                },
                {
                  "type": "progress_ring",
                  "value": "60",
                  "size": "140",
                  "stroke_width": "10",
                  "color": "#4f46e5",
                  "label": "Cards reviewed",
                  "show_value": "true",
                  "unit": "%"
                },
                {
                  "type": "progress_bar",
                  "value": 60,
                  "label": "Reviewed",
                  "accent": "#4f46e5",
                  "show_percent": "true",
                  "caption": "6 of 10 cards reviewed · 4 remaining"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text_callout",
                  "variant": "info",
                  "title": "How to review",
                  "description": "Say the meaning out loud before you flip. If you got it right, move on; if not, revisit the card at the end of the deck."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
]
</a2ui-json>

The progress ring and bar show a snapshot of 6 of 10 reviewed. This catalog's flashcard deck exposes no data binding, so the progress panel can't update itself as cards are flipped. To reflect real progress, send updated `value` and `caption` figures after each review.
